# Copy to .env — never commit .env itself (see devops/.gitignore).
#
# The single public origin this whole deployment is reachable at — the URL a BROWSER uses to
# reach the Gateway, not any internal container hostname. Two things read this:
#   - devops/observability/docker-compose.yml's grafana service (GF_SERVER_ROOT_URL) — Grafana is
#     served from this origin's /admin/grafana sub-path via the Gateway's tool-proxy, so it needs
#     to know its own externally-visible URL or its rendered asset/API links break.
#   - devops/frontend/docker-compose.yml's frontend build (passed through frontend/Dockerfile as
#     EXPO_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_ORIGIN, which frontend/src/config/urls.js reads) — every API/WS call the
#     app makes targets this origin.
#
# Change this ONE value to change both — e.g. to a real domain before a non-local deployment.
# devops/observability is a separate Compose project from devops/ (different directory, different
# `docker compose` invocation) — its startup command needs an explicit
# `--env-file ../.env` flag to pick up this same file; see CLAUDE.md/.claude/agents/devops.md for
# the full startup sequence.
PUBLIC_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8000
